# Pull requests

Never push commits to `master` (or `main`). Use a feature branch and open a PR against `master`.

Every PR uses `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`. Fill it in. Do not open a blank PR.

1. **Title** — one line, why the change exists
2. **Summary** — 1–3 bullets of what changed
3. **Test plan** — a short checklist (CI, a signed-in flow, an edge case)

```markdown
## Summary
- …

## Test plan
- [ ] CI `lint, type-check, test` passes
- [ ] …
```

Pass that body to `gh pr create`. If `gh` cannot open the PR, put the same body on the compare URL. Do not leave a branch with no description of how to test it.
